        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2: img2img\n\n[Krea 2](https://huggingface.co/krea/Krea-2-Turbo) (Krea, Qwen3-VL 4B text encoder, Qwen-Image VAE) is an aesthetic\ntext-to-image model. **Turbo** (`krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors`, set here) is the 8-step TDM-distilled variant;\n**Raw** (`krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors`) is the undistilled base and runs in the same graph, see below.\n\n**Settings (Turbo)**: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple, 1024×1024 (up to 2048×2048). At CFG 1 there is no negative\npass, so the negative prompt has no effect. **CFG above 1 degrades the image.**\n\n**Prompts**: full descriptive sentences (subject, setting, composition, lighting, materials, mood), not tag\nlists. Stay well under ~500 tokens: very long prompts produce black images. `(word:1.2)` weights are not\nknown to work.\n\n## Raw\n\n**Raw** is the checkpoint LoRAs and fine-tunes are trained on, with the widest variety and a real negative prompt. It\nis much slower than Turbo. Choose `krea2_raw_fp8_scaled` in the model list and set about 52 steps and CFG 3.5 (true\nCFG: two passes per step). Krea gives no sampler or scheduler for Raw:\neuler / simple are a starting point. The negative prompt works at CFG 3.5; keep it short or leave it empty.\n\n## img2img\n\nThe image of **Load Image ib:img** is the starting point: **Resize to** scales it to the size of the Generate tab\n(Width / Height, its *Resize to* in img2img mode; **Use size** in the Input cell takes the size of the image),\n**VAE Encode** makes the latent, and the sampler adds noise by the **denoising** strength (0.6 here) and samples\nfrom there. The prompt describes the whole image you want. Low denoising keeps the composition and colors; high\ndenoising moves further from the image. To change one area only, use the inpaint workflow; to change the image by\nan instruction, an edit model with references.\n\nThe Generate tab is in **img2img** mode while this workflow is loaded. Send an image with **Send to the input\nimage** (B), from the editor, or upload it in the Input cell before the first queue. This workflow has no Hires.\nfix pass: upscale the result with the full workflow.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; Send to the input image (B), the editor |\n| `ib:pp` / `ib:np` | Image Bench Prompt / Negative Prompt | prompts and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale (CFG), sampling method, schedule type; denoising; Resize to (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt; the **Image Bench Prompt** node\napplies them. **Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses it again.\n\n**Style LoRAs** ([Comfy-Org/Krea-2/loras](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/loras), strength 1.0) need\ntheir trigger words in the prompt, e.g. `<lora:krea2_darkbrush:1> monochrome ink wash style` (`darkbrush`: monochrome\nink wash style, `dotmatrix`: monochrome stippling style, `kidsdrawing`: naive expressive sketch style, `neondrip`:\ntextured abstract style, `rainywindow`: rainy window style, `retroanime`: purple retro anime style, `softwatercolor`:\nart deco watercolor style, `sunsetblur`: ethereal motion blur style, `vintagetarot`: vintage tarot style).\n\nThe Generate tab has no References panel and the ControlNet tab no units: the stock nodes take no reference images\nfor Krea 2 (the Identity Edit and Style Reference LoRAs need their own node packs), and its control LoRAs are not\nControlNets.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2) also has `*_bf16` and `*_int8_convrot` diffusion models of\nRaw and Turbo, `krea2_turbo_mxfp8` / `krea2_turbo_nvfp4` (RTX 50), and the bf16 / int8 text encoders.\n\n**diffusion_models**: [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors), [krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (one file for Raw and Turbo)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) (the Qwen-Image VAE)\n**loras**: [krea2_darkbrush.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/loras/krea2_darkbrush.safetensors)\n\nKrea 2 is released under the Krea 2 Community License."
      ],
      "title": "Note: Krea 2 (Image Bench, img2img)",
